I agree fully with your analysis, but I disagree with the intended (and
functional) result.  A fifth-level monster hitting AC -20 with a 1 in 4
chance???  Give me a break!  A fifth-level character could _never_ hit
a monster with AC -20 (not from source, just experience...)  In fact,
there was one poster who said that his 6th (7th?) level Samurai missed
a killer bee for over 200 turns in a row, and since a killer bee has only
an AC of -4, there is an enormous discrepancy.  The Samurai would need at
least a +5 katana (for 25% chance to hit, assuming he was at +0, 0%
chance to hit) and AC -20 to be even with a 5th level monster with AC -4.

I want a linear, NOT slowly asymptotic, scale like the ones the monsters
strike at, with a min of 5%.

